{
  "title": "AuthenticatedImageLoader re-downloads every image on every \
appearance",
  "description": "`AuthenticatedImageLoader` has no memory or disk cache and \
`onDisappear` cancels the in-flight task. Scrolling a long recipe list or \
flipping between tabs re-fetches every thumbnail over HTTPS + bearer auth. \
SwiftUI's `AsyncImage` at least uses `URLCache.shared`. Options: (1) attach \
`URLCache` to the authenticated session, (2) keep a process-level \
`NSCache<URL, UIImage>` keyed by URL, (3) use `CachedAsyncImage` / \
`Kingfisher`. A simple in-memory cache would already eliminate most \
re-fetches.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "performance",
  ],
